1253:
It shall be unlawful for any person to establish racks or stands for vending goods on the streets, public squares, parks or alleys of the city, without the consent of the city council first obtained, or pursuant to the following conditions for sidewalk displays located in the Central Business District zoning district:
(1) Sidewalk displays of merchandise in the city Central Business District. A sidewalk display of merchandise may be conducted on a public sidewalk by a retail or wholesale business in the Central Business District (CBD zoning district) without a permit or prior consent of city council under the following conditions for sidewalks located in the Central Business District (CBD zoning district) zoning district:
a. The display shall be situated so as to abut the facade of the building (as defined in the City's Zoning Ordinance) in which the business selling the displayed merchandise is located and shall not obstruct building entrances, fire exits, utility meters, cellar entrances, or standpipes or other safety equipment;
b. The display shall not exceed a size of 36 inches in depth and 72 inches in height. The display shall cover not more than one-half of the length of the front wall of said business.
c. The provision of paragraph(b) above notwithstanding, an area of not less than five feet of unobstructed pedestrian passageway shall be maintained at all times between any display and the nearest curb, tree, pole or other permanent object situate in the right-of-way;
d. The display shall consist only of fungible merchandise regularly sold in the ordinary course of the business displaying the merchandise; and no signs, advertisements or other written or graphic material(except such merchandise sold in the ordinary course of the business maintaining the display) may be posted or placed on a sidewalk display;
e. The following items are prohibited in any display: tobacco products, alcoholic beverages, obscene material as defined by O.C.G.A. § 16-12-80, weapons, live animals or pawned items;
f. All sidewalk displays as provided for in this section shall be removed from the sidewalk during any time when the business displaying such merchandise is closed to customers;
g. All final sales transactions between business and customer shall be conducted within the business establishment, not on the sidewalk;
h. Any person or business conducting sidewalk displays shall not cause any loud or offensive noise, either from his or her person or from any device, instrument or equipment for the purpose of attracting attention to such display or to the sale of any goods or merchandise;
i. No person or business shall display goods or merchandise directly on the ground, or on any cloth, plastic or similar ground covering on any sidewalk or other public right-of-way. All displays must be stabilized with no risk of overturning due to wind or incidental contact.
j. No display shall block the sidewalk or in any way interfere with the requirements of the American with Disabilities Act.
k. Notwithstanding the provisions of section 18-7(1)b. hereinabove, during specific city sponsored events, the display may extend the entire length of the facade of the building of said business.
(2) Penalties. Violation of this section 18-7, upon conviction, shall be punishable by a fine not to exceed $1,000.00 per violation and/or imprisonment not to exceed 60 days. Each day a business owner violates this section 18-7 shall constitute a separate offense.
(Code 1972, § 24-7; Ord. No. 15-8, § I, 7-21-15)

